Apple is releasing two new products today, Friday, November 13: the all-new Apple HomeView and the fourth-generation Apple TV 4K, both of which have been available to pre-order since mid-October.<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-pro-tell-logo.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071590" /><br/>
<ul><li><strong>Apple HomeView</strong>: Apple's new smart home display, powered by Apple Intelligence with Siri AI, for entertainment and managing the home. Available in tabletop and wall-mounted models, it can recognize up to six users by face, each with a personalized Home Screen. The HomeView is priced at &#36;299.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Apple TV 4K</strong>: adds Siri AI, the A19 chip, an updated Siri Remote with Find My, and support for four-speaker surround sound with HomePod mini 2. The Apple TV 4K comes with 128GB of storage and is priced at &#36;299.</li></ul>Both products were announced on October 13 alongside the HomePod mini 2, which launched October 30. <br/>
